+      "response": "\"The Arab Tent\" is an oil\u2011on\u2011canvas by the English Victorian painter Edwin (Henry) Landseer, dated around 1865\u201366. It was shown at the Royal Academy in 1866 under the title \u201cMare and Foal \u2013 Indian Tent\u2026,\u201d though the tent depicted is clearly Arab. The composition features an Arab mare with her foal, two Persian greyhounds, and two monkeys (one wearing an earring), with the owner hinted at by a pair of pipes in a jar on the right.\n\nThe work passed from the Prince of Wales (who bought it in 1867) to Sir Richard Wallace in 1878 for \u00a36,300, making it one of the most expensive early acquisitions for the Wallace Collection. Today it hangs in the Hall, and its recent conservation in 2017 was supported by Henrietta, Duchess of Bedford.",
